<<~ ahu #head >>

! Persona-Circle ~ the human as a Circle of selves

A human reads not as one identity but as a ''private Circle of context-selves'' — Plurality Pono made literal in the identity plane, the identity instance of [[multi-fractal]]. The model lives entirely on the ''WHO plane'' (membership/identity); the INFRA plane (transport/carriage) stays orthogonal and untouched here. <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture >>

Triple-cruci­bled (local canon · the operator's recorded design · the deep-knowledge web): the spine restates held canon, the overclaims got cut.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #two-axes >>

!! The Two Axes ~ composition ⊥ disclosure

The WHO plane re-cuts into two ''orthogonal'' axes (the same de-fusing move [[causal-islands]] ran on its ladder — never a new linear ladder):

* ''COMPOSITION (structural, bottom-up emergent):'' `vessel~veil` binding → ''handle-Circle'' (PersonaGroup) → ''the Vault'' (the human's private namespace over its handles — NEVER a published Circle; #the-vault). The cardinality joins ARE the structure — but the top join ''collects, never merges'': a group that //names// its members links them, so the human's own selves are held in a private namespace, off every roster.
* ''DISCLOSURE (a per-join DIAL, not a tier):'' veiled ↔ known. One continuous //linkability// axis (Pfitzmann–Hansen: anonymity ↔ accountability, pseudonymity the whole span). It applies at ''each join independently'' — a vessel, a handle, the human, each veiled or named in any combination.

The earlier error fused them — labelling the boundaries "anon vs known" when the real boundaries are the cardinality joins. //Which hearth// (composition) and //how-linkable// (disclosure) ask different questions. The veil is not "anon petname relabeled" — it is the disclosure axis, on which ''anon = name⊥''.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #the-atom >>

!! The Atom ~ a `vessel~veil` binding, two keys

The base atom carries ''two keys'' (Veilid's peer-identity ⊥ user-identity, a real two-axis = substrate ≠ sovereignty rendered as keys):

* ''vessel-key'' — the device/substrate identity. ''DEVICE-MINTED, forged on its own device, the private half never leaving'' (#vessel-key doctrine; admit-by-signing-never-by-sharing). It is ''NEVER derived from the persona seed'' — deriving it would be the ''copy-the-key antipattern'' that dissolves per-device revocation (Veilid/SSB). It is a //local substrate secret// and ''MUST NEVER co-surface'' (sign-alongside / share-route / time-correlate) with the veiled-user-key.
* ''veiled-user-key'' — the sovereign pseudonym presented through the veil. This is the ''anon user-pseudonym'' — a binding whose name is ⊥ until disclosed.

This adds a //new// cut beside the existing per-vessel Ed25519-sign ⊥ X25519-KEM cut (#four-port-swap); it does not restate it.

''THE TRUE NAME MODEL ~ how the atoms bind without merging.'' The atom holds its two keys apart; a ''signed edge'' is what joins atoms — never shared key material. ''BIND BY EDGE, NEVER BY SEED.'' The alternative fails at the substrate: a key ''copied'' between vessels //is// the collector, presented to every verifier it meets, landing on ''merge'' by the single-bit test (#the-vault) and linking every self beneath any policy written above it. The edge binds AT the hearth's True Name, which is why a Place must hold a name of its own (<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes >>).

''The edge runs SIDEWAYS, never downward'' (operator ruling — the inversion-of-control eigenstate). Each ''device+veil atom stands as a LOCAL IDENTITY'' in its own right, and the worn veil ''changes at will''. The ''PersonaGroup COLLECTS'' those atoms that share a pet-name for the human into an ''identity-FLEET'' — it does not grant them, does not own them, and stands as no root above them. A fleet reads as ''what the atoms declare when they name each other'' (<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/group-as-closure >> — //"no edge speaks for another member"//). So an edge that runs only root→device names a ''hierarchy'', never this fleet; the pono form carries ''both halves, each signed by its own subject'', and membership resolves as the reciprocal-edge closure rather than a pinned grant.

''INTERNAL ⊥ EXTERNAL — the hard law.'' The fleet's ''internal'' identity — the pet-name declaring //these atoms are one hand// — ''NEVER equals'' the ''external'' identity the operator publishes as a Handle. The collector stays inside; the face goes out; ''no act may collapse them to one value''. That is #the-vault's single bit read at the fleet scale: publish the face, never the fleet.

''One seed, persona-side only.'' The ''veiled-user / persona'' keys derive from ONE seed via ''ed25519 HD-derivation, all-hardened paths'' — recover the seed, re-derive the whole persona constellation; ed25519-HD is structurally immune to the xpub-linkage trap (SLIP-0010 = hardened-only). The ''vessel-key stays outside the seed'' (device-minted). So recovery is cheap on the persona side without fusing substrate sovereignty. <<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lararium-identity >>

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #composition >>

!! Composition ~ emergent Circles (inversion of control)

The joins above the atom are ''emergent Circles — the closure of MUTUAL bindings, constituted bottom-up, never granted by a root'' (the operator's Josh-Ellis "Circles" / Kowloon inversion-of-control; canon's `group-as-closure`). A Circle is not a thing //instead of// bindings — ''a Circle IS what mutual bindings declare'' when they hold each other back.

* ''handle-Circle (PersonaGroup)'' — the closure of vessels mutually holding one ''handle ↔ DID'' (the AT-Proto/Nostr pattern: a //mutable// handle over a //stable// DID, bound by ''bidirectional proof'', the human-readable form never on the wire). A "Known Handle with multiple vessels."
* ''me-Circle (a compartment of the human)'' — the self-held, ''single-principal'', private constellation of the handles in ONE compartment (= a Vault, #the-vault). Disclosed edge-by-edge, never wholesale: ''no global self.'' A human keeps ''MANY'' me-Circles, mutually unlinkable (Senior-Engineer ⊥ Guru ⊥ Telarus-KSC); a single me-Circle over //all// a human's handles would be the Nymwars root, so the "me" is the compartment, never the whole person. RULED (operator, myth-as-spec, witnessed load-bearing): a me-Circle composes as ''an imagined expanse in l-space where the Personas OVERLAP'' — //a single-principal cabal-realm.// The ''same realm machinery'' (found · contract · the capture-clock), with the multi-principal complexity ''degenerate to trivial'' (one ordering authority: you → no tie-break engages · capture-immune, you cannot capture your own me · no legitimacy contest). ''One Persona takes the blame at a time'' (the Voice-house pattern: one face surfaces, named; switching is free, single-principal). The embodied human ''carries the realm through space-time'' (body + environment = the carriage). Composition (//who is me//, the Circle) ⊥ the optional shared substrate (//what me maintains//, the realm); a me with no shared docs stays pure Circle, a me that syncs state founds the cardinality-1 realm. Witnessed: `me-circle.ts` (8/8) + the real-Keyhive `me-circle-lifecycle` probe (the clock shows spread=30, the me reads capture-immune).

Convergence across a Circle runs ''only on mutual contract'' — the handshake IS the key-agreement ([[contract-as-key-agreement]], `convergent-mesh`).

!!! The multi-principal tie-break — PROPOSED, the operator's seat

Pure inversion-of-control ''breaks at the multi-principal key-handover'': with equal peers and no-global-now, a concurrent add-while-remove can leak a key, and every shipped sound system (p2panda-auth, Keyhive) keeps a seniority/root asymmetry to order it. The Mu cut:

* ''Single-principal Circles take NO break'' — the me-Circle and a one-human handle-Circle (your own devices) have one ordering authority: //you//. That is sovereignty over your own constellation, not a top-down root. ''The personal constellation holds under pure IoC.''
* ''Multi-principal Circles (Kowloon Cabals)'' need a tie-break — ''either'' a ''kahu the Circle constitutes for itself'' (the constitutional-core role, elected by mutual contract, revocable — IoC-compatible, not a re-collapsed root) ''or'' ''accept-and-heal'' (a narrow leak window, healed by key-rotation + the cost-dial below). //Awaiting the operator's seat.//

''The concern narrows to that ONE window.'' Witnessed (`cabal-two-human`, 3/3): two DIFFERENT humans on a LAN, no shared metal, ride BeeKEM through a cabal under ''bounded concurrency'' — concurrent CONTENT converges (each reads the post the other made without seeing it first), and concurrent ADD+ADD survives (both admit a third at once, no crash). So a small, low-churn cabal shares content on CGKA today (as `dreamnet-architecture` already rules: cabal membership scopes read). The tie-break governs ONLY the concurrent add-''while''-remove key-leak the line above names — never multi-principal sharing at large. The add-while-remove leak — the very window this seat exists for — was probed (`cabal-two-human`, 5/5) and does NOT manifest for a two-human cabal: keyhive REFUSES a revoke ''up'' the chain (a member cannot revoke its own delegator — "Proof missing to authorize revocation"), and an authorized revoke cleanly excludes the removed member even RACING a concurrent add (removed member reads nothing after its removal). So ''accept-and-heal (BeeKEM's native rekey) suffices'' for the two-human window; the kahu stays optional — reserved for larger or higher-churn cabals where deeper concurrency may still bite. One honest un-probed edge remains: a member added through a CONFLICTED-root double-add may need a conflict-key retry to read.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #disclosure >>

!! Disclosure ~ the per-join dial, and its gate

''Anon is the base; a known handle is a disclosure act'' (Nissenbaum's contextual integrity — staying veiled in a context is //appropriate flow//, ''never a deficit or an un-climbed ladder''). Lifting the veil is ''reversible toward-veiled'' (the linkage ''erodes'' back to the anon floor; anergy-not-ban — and note the shape: no lease is held and none lapses, since a lease reads as a substance-object carried between exercises. What decays is the DWELLING, `nohopapa`-wise: stop feeding the linkage and it wears down, leaving no deed behind. `identity-enacts-relation#the-constructor`) — but a ''severed'' past does NOT re-weld: kāpae is remove-wins, re-linking a cut identity is irreversible and costly ([[kapae]]). Graduate by ''transferring a credential to a fresh pseudonym'' (Chaum), never by proving sameness, so the veil can re-close on a new key. ''BUILT'' (`veil-crossing.ts`): the crossing is a per-join gesture — ''LIFT'' (keep the anon key, link, carry the reputation — the anon past //welds//) or ''HOLD'' (refound a fresh key at a new all-hardened path — no back-link a wire-watcher can follow, //severed//). The mechanism serves either anon-key policy (stable-reused vs ephemeral — the operator's recorded fork); the ''ZK-vouch'' (a refound blessed by someone who knew the anon, //without// the public link) stays the adjacent arc.

''The Sybil gate at the Circle-join'' is the operator's designed ''voucher cost-dial'': marginal-not-absolute (`rb>c`, the voucher supplies r), the ''voucher co-pays AND becomes the watcher'', ''anergy-not-ban'' (no vouch → stay at the anon floor, re-presentable), slashing-by-revocation. The pledge is a ''WHO-plane edge'' (who-vouches-for-whom) — the planes stay clean. It ''prices'' Sybil, never eliminates it. ''The mechanism is BUILT'' (`veil-vouch.ts`): a voucher carries ''DECAYED rep across a HOLD'' (`carryRepAcrossHold`: stake × decay, < 1 → no free teleport; the rep rides the VOUCHER edge, the fresh key stays public-unlinkable), guarded by a ''one-time nullifier'' (= an epoch-lease slot — blocks sever-and-refound rep-farming). Left OPEN, the operator's forks: the ''dial numbers'' (decay-rate · stake-fraction) ride as parameters; ''one-kahu-vs-threshold'' blind-oracle + the actual ''ZK blind-signature'' (certify without knowing which vessel — the Identity-Continuity Paradox: someone holds the link) stay the deferred crypto layer.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #the-vault >>

!! The Vault ~ the collector is a secret, never a group

''Four blind domains converge (HD wallets · anonymous credentials · group-key agreement · petname/SDSI''
''naming): the layer that knows "all these handles are me" is a SECRET, held private, and it must NEVER be a''
''published group.''

* ''HD wallets'' ship it as the Monero ''view key'' — one secret recognises a thousand unlinkable
  subaddresses, holds no spend authority, publishes no link.
* ''Anonymous credentials'' hold it as the ''master secret'' (Chaum 1985; Camenisch–Lysyanskaya 2001) —
  its knowledge is //exactly// what the unlinkability proof withholds from everyone else.
* ''Naming'' calls it a ''private namespace / petname book'' (SDSI, RFC 2693; Stiegler) — //a NAMESPACE,//
//  not a super-key.// A key placed over the handles becomes a presentable root that correlates them.
* ''Group crypto'' proves the wall (RFC 9420; Keyhive): //co-members cannot hide co-membership from each//
//  other//, so the handles MUST NOT share a roster.

''The single-bit test — collect vs merge:'' //is the collector ever PUBLISHED or PRESENTED to a verifier?//
Local-only → ''collect'' (unlinkable). Published → ''merge'' (links every self). That one bit is the whole
architecture, and its violation is the ''Nymwars harm'' (Google+/Facebook real-name, 2011–14): a forced
single-legal-name root de-pseudonymised activists, performers, survivors — //the presented root became the//
//correlation key.// And the ''OIDC-IdP'' lesson: keep the collector on the human's own device, NEVER a shared
party who holds the master table.

''A Vault IS a me-Circle, seen from the key layer.'' The me-Circle (#composition) names the collector as a
//place in l-space where a human's chosen Personas overlap//; the Vault names the //same// collector as the
private secret that derives them. Both hold the load-bearing property — ''single-principal, never''
''wholesale-disclosed, no global self.'' The place-framing and the key-framing agree.

''A human holds MANY vaults / me-Circles, each a compartment, deliberately unlinkable even from each other.''
Senior-Engineer-Josh ⊥ Guru-Josh ⊥ Telarus-KSC — ''separate seeds, separate namespaces'', and ''NOTHING''
''stands above them that links them'' (a layer above the vaults would BE the Nymwars root). A single me-Circle
over //all// a human's handles IS that root — so a me-Circle collects the handles of ONE compartment, and the
human keeps as many compartments as their life demands. The vault stands at the top; the meat-brain holds the
only join between compartments, and it never rides any wire.

''A vessel joins each handle-group under a PER-HANDLE PSEUDONYMOUS CREDENTIAL, never its raw device key.'' A
vessel that joins by its ''immutable device key'' puts that one key on every handle-group's roster, so two
handles on one device share a roster entry — and by the co-membership law (RFC 9420; Keyhive), anyone in
either group ''links them''. The credential is DERIVED per handle: the deck stays one deck; the face it wears
differs per handle, and no roster carries a key that appears on another.

''THE UPGRADE — the nym must PROVE itself, not merely look unlinkable.'' SLIP-0010 `handle'/context'`
derivation is right in //shape// and unverifiable in //fact//: a relying party cannot check the derivation, cannot
enforce one-nym-per-scope, cannot bind a credential to the seed. The sharper primitive rides beside it —
''scope-exclusive pseudonyms'' `nym = PRF_s(scope)` proven in zero-knowledge (Dodis–Yampolskiy VRF, or
Hash-DH / ISO 20008-2), bound to the same committed master secret. Keep SLIP-0010 as the //local// tree; let the
NETWORK-facing nym be the ZK-proven scope pseudonym. Then verifiable · per-scope sybil-bounded ·
credential-linkable — the three things bare derivation cannot assert — and ''the vault falls out for free,''
''because it IS the committed secret.''

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #honest-scope >>

!! Honest Scope ~ the key layer only

The model closes ''only the key layer'' — and there it closes well: unlinkable-by-construction at the //key// layer on ed25519-HD. It does ''NOT'' deliver cross-self unlinkability against an observer who sees the wire, the disclosed credentials, or the prose:

* ''disclosure-protocol'' — the graduate move is now BUILT (lift/hold veil-crossing, #disclosure). The richer //selective//-disclosure is a SOLVED, standard-track primitive: ''BBS'' signatures (IRTF CFRG standard-track — reveal a subset, prove the rest in a re-randomised, unlinkable presentation) and ''Coconut'' (NDSS 2019 — //threshold// issuance, t-of-n authorities, no single trusted issuer, which fits a causal-island confederation exactly). Adopt over the surface; the primitive is solved. The ZK-vouch stays owed.
* ''transport'' — OPEN (mixnet/private-routing territory; do not lean on it as solved). The wallet literature confirms the boundary: de-anonymisation is graph/behavioral (Meiklejohn; Möser), //never a key break// — the keys were never the leak.
* ''behavioral'' — OPEN (fingerprint/stylometry defeat key hygiene; crypto cannot touch it).
* ''the collector leaks below the key layer'' — the handles being unlinkable-by-key is NECESSARY, never SUFFICIENT. The link re-enters through everything the selves SHARE beneath the keys: a published roster (SSB metafeeds //list// subfeeds), a shared substrate (container tabs isolate cookies, never IP/fingerprint), a shared relay/IdP, correlated timing, or a ''Janus'' interactive-receipt probe. A "switch/manage between handles" flow MUST NOT become a Janus oracle.

''Sybil scarcity lives OUTSIDE the math.'' Every field agreed: pseudonym crypto gives //one-nym-per-scope// only — one master secret mints unbounded nyms across DIFFERENT scopes, and no pairing substitutes for scarce enrollment. Global scarcity needs an external root, and in this stack that root IS the ''vouch-lineage'' (#the-siege-gate, lar:///…/admission-on-a-lineage) — the proof-of-personhood the crypto proves it cannot supply alone.

And the substrate itself, by canon, has ''no forward-secrecy and no retroactive revocation'' — a leaked vessel-key reads all its history; //that fact IS the security posture// (#four-port-swap). Claiming "no observer can link the selves" would be Confabulation-as-Canon. The truthful claim: ''the key layer is solved and unlinkable-by-construction on ed25519-HD; transport and behavioral ride separate, open machinery.''

